  "label": "Nazi Fitness Camp Stereotype",
  "description": "A hateful and historically inaccurate stereotype that equates modern fitness or bodybuilding with the forced physical conditioning and racial ideology of the Nazi regime. This is a deliberate and offensive misrepresentation used to dehumanize or stigmatize individuals or groups, particularly in the context of bodybuilding or fitness culture. It relies on the historical trauma of the Holocaust and Nazi atrocities to trivialize or mock contemporary physical transformation.",
